{
  "_comment": [
    "Default read-timeout values per service, from the cross-SDK default-timeouts program.",
    "This mirrors the shared artifact that aws-sdk-go-v2 and aws-sdk-java-v2 also check in;",
    "the `services` map is kept key-for-key identical to theirs so the three stay diffable.",
    "",
    "Units are milliseconds. -1 means no read timeout is applied to that service at all.",
    "A service absent from `services` gets `generalDefaultMillis`.",
    "",
    "Rust applies the general default to three services this list fully exempts, because Rust's",
    "read timeout closes once response headers arrive and so cannot fire mid-stream. Those",
    "overrides live in codegen, in TimeoutDefaults.kt, not here, so that this file remains a",
    "faithful copy of the shared data."
  ],
  "generalDefaultMillis": 300000,
